"""Original bilingual authored setting; no source-world text is reused."""
REGIONS = [
('烬河边疆','Ashriver Frontier','旧帝国的税道止于河岸。镇民靠摆渡、磨坊与小块农地过冬，五大势力各有来客，却没有谁能单独养活这里。','The old imperial tax road ends at the river. Ferries, mills and small farms feed the settlements. All five powers have visitors here, but none can sustain the frontier alone.'),
('断旗高地','Brokenbanner Highlands','战后的军户与牧人共用旧营垒。所谓王国边界，在放羊的人眼里常只是一条缺了桥的溪。','Veteran households and shepherds share abandoned fortifications. To a shepherd, a disputed royal border is often only a stream whose bridge has fallen.'),
('沉钟林地','Sunkenbell Woodlands','林中的钟先于人类王朝。树木会留下火与斧的痕迹，却不会替任何阵营说谎或作证。','The forest bells predate human dynasties. Trees retain marks of fire and axes; they do not automatically testify for any faction.'),
('铜脊山系','Copperback Mountains','矮人深炉诸家并非一个国王的臣民。矿权、通风、水源和工人家属，使每一场争端都比一块金属复杂。','The dwarven Deephearth Houses share no single king. Mining rights, ventilation, water and workers’ families make every dispute larger than a lump of metal.'),
('九塔湖区','Nine-Tower Lakes','九塔是合议学社，不是九位全知贤者。学徒给渔户修水泵，渔户告诉学徒哪里不宜取水。','The Nine Towers are a scholarly council, not nine omniscient sages. Apprentices repair fishing pumps; fishers teach them where water should not be drawn.'),
('无名王庭','The Nameless Court','没有人还握有完整帝国档案。旧城有人卖面包，有人在废墟中认祖，也有人宁愿祖辈的事继续埋着。','No one holds the complete imperial archives. Bakers still work in the old city, families search its ruins for their past, and others prefer that past buried.'),
('雾湾海岸','Mistbay Coast','渔民、难民和商船都等待同一阵顺风。古灯塔虽被帝国编入航路，却比帝国更古老。','Fishers, refugees and traders wait for the same favorable wind. Imperial navigators adopted the ancient beacons, but never built their deepest foundations.'),
('灰穗平原','Greygrain Plain','麦田不是争王者的空白棋盘。佃农、自由农、兽裔牧群和流动工匠彼此依赖，也争夺有限的干燥仓房。','Fields are not empty squares on a claimant’s board. Tenants, free farmers, beastkin herders and traveling artisans depend on one another while competing for dry granaries.')]
# name, English name, scene, scene EN, livelihood/problem, EN, opportunity/boundary, EN
LOCATIONS = [
('渡鸦桥镇','Ravenbridge','黑石桥上有七只生锈的铁鸦，桥下水轮整夜转动，面包房天亮前亮灯。','Seven rusting iron ravens line the black bridge; waterwheels turn all night, and the bakery lights before dawn.','桥费养着修桥工，难民觉得收费偏向商队，镇议事厅还没谈妥冬季减免。','Tolls pay the bridge crew. Refugees say merchants receive favors; winter exemptions remain unsettled.','客栈、桥工棚与集市各有人做主。能卸货挣钱、问路学艺，也可不理公示板先找住处。','The inn, bridge yard and market have different keepers. Earn unloading wages, ask about training, or simply find a bed.'),
('三盏灯客栈','Three Lamps Inn','三盏灯一盏照门，一盏照灶，一盏留给晚归的人；兽裔与人类常共一张长桌。','One lamp lights the door, one the stove, and one waits for late arrivals; humans and beastkin share long tables.','掌柜欠磨坊一批面粉钱，却照常给桥工留热汤。','The innkeeper owes the mill for flour but still saves hot soup for bridge workers.','打听传闻不等于获准翻客房；借宿、洗衣、约见与送信都可由普通交往展开。','Rumors do not grant access to bedrooms. Lodging, laundry, meetings and letters belong to ordinary social life.'),
('旧税关','Old Tollhouse','帝国鹰徽被柴烟熏黑，查验台上压着自由盟的新印和一叠未销的旧税票。','Soot blackens the imperial eagle; a Free League seal rests beside uncanceled imperial tax slips.','关吏发现两批粮车持相同编号，可能是伪造，也可能是旧表误抄。','Two grain wagons carry the same receipt number: forgery and clerical error are both possible.','可比较实物与证言，或代送账副；没看过的账页不会因会算术自动成为已知证据。','Compare records and witnesses or deliver a copy. Numeracy does not reveal pages you have never seen.'),
('磨石渡','Millstone Ferry','平底渡船擦着磨石旁的回水靠岸，河泥里留下被拖走的长木痕。','Flat-bottomed ferries land beside a millstone eddy; long timber drag marks cross the mud.','渡工想加班运木，河对岸村民担心上游伐木堵了鱼汛。','Boat crews want timber work; villagers across the river fear upstream logging will spoil the fish run.','摆渡有实际行程，暴涨时可以等水、绕道或帮修缆；没有免费跨河的聊天捷径。','Crossings take travel time. During floods, wait, detour or repair the cable; conversation is no free river crossing.'),
('灰烬田','Ash Fields','去年焚毁的麦垛边长出新荞麦，一只缝补多次的风车吱吱响。','New buckwheat grows beside last year’s burned ricks, beneath a repeatedly patched windmill.','农户争执谁该修共用水渠，受伤的退伍兵仍想守住自己的田。','Neighbors dispute who repairs the shared irrigation ditch; an injured veteran wants to keep his plot.','收割、灌溉与照看牲畜都能成为生活；寻到旧军械也先问土地与遗物归谁。','Harvesting and animal care are real work. A discovered weapon cache still has landowners and possible heirs.'),
('白砾驿','Whitegravel Post','换马院的白石被蹄铁磨平，信使在门边晾湿披风，窗内传来棋子声。','Hooves polish the pale stones of the relay yard; couriers dry cloaks outside a room full of chess talk.','一位信使失联，替班的人不愿接夜路，却未必是在隐瞒罪行。','One courier is missing. His replacement refuses the night route, which is not proof of guilt.','寄信需有收件去处与递送时间；认识远方的人不表示能直接在脑中联系。','Letters need a destination and delivery time. Knowing someone far away does not create telepathy.'),
('断旗堡','Brokenbanner Keep','城垛上十二面旧旗拼成防雨布，操场上有木剑、军用锅和晾晒的襁褓。','Twelve old banners form a rain awning over wooden swords, army kettles and drying swaddles.','白棘骑士团驻守一翼，军户住另一翼；团长的粮秣命令必须面对居民的冬粮。','The White Thorn Order holds one wing and military families another; supply orders compete with winter food.','有明确同意才能切磋；入团是立场与义务，不会自动领取全堡装备。','Sparring requires consent. Joining means obligations and affiliation, not ownership of the armory.'),
('白棘演武场','White Thorn Yard','木桩缠着布条，栏杆外有磨剑摊和帮伤者换绷带的棚子。','Cloth wraps the practice posts, with a sword grinder and bandaging shelter outside the rail.','教头要让新兵学会停手，年轻骑士却只想当众赢一次。','The instructor teaches recruits when to stop; a young knight wants one public victory.','可练盾、长刃、急救并交相应材料费用，武艺不因观看一次就掌握。','Study shields, blades or first aid with proper sources and costs; watching once grants no mastery.'),
('断誓礼拜堂','Broken Oath Chapel','彩窗只剩蓝色碎片，唱诗台下摆着一箱寄不出去的军人家书。','Only blue fragments remain in the stained glass; undeliverable soldiers’ letters sit beneath the choir.','祭司要安葬无名死者，堡中书记坚持先核名字，双方都怕有人被抹去。','A priest seeks burial for unknown dead; a clerk asks for names first. Both fear erasure.','祈祷可安慰人，不能凭空复活；疗伤依真实能力、材料和伤情处理。','Prayer may comfort; it cannot invent resurrection. Healing follows actual skill, supplies and injury.'),
('红砂隘口','Red Sand Pass','风把红砂吹进铠甲接缝，商队用石头压住地上的临时路条。','Wind drives red sand into armor joints; merchants weigh temporary passes down with stones.','守军追查失窃马匹，走私者夹在合法商队中，不能见货车就当敌人。','Guards seek stolen horses; smugglers hide among lawful wagons, not every wagon is an enemy.','查证、护送、绕行都可能成立，真实交战才进入战斗。','Investigation, escort and detours are possible; only real hostilities become combat.'),
('悬草坡','Hanginggrass Slope','长草从悬崖垂下，山羊铃声先于牧人出现在薄雾里。','Long grasses spill over cliffs; goat bells arrive through the mist before their owners.','兽裔牧民与堡中军需争草场，双方各有病弱牲畜要活过冬天。','Beastkin herders and army suppliers contest pasture while both nurse vulnerable animals.','可以照料、调解或寻找替代草场；一个族群不会因一人得罪你便全体仇视。','Care, mediation and alternate pasture are options; one dispute does not make an entire people hostile.'),
('倒旗墓道','Fallen Banner Crypt','石阶向下没入潮气，一面没有纹章的军旗盖着未封棺的木框。','Damp steps descend past an unmarked banner over an unfinished coffin frame.','军需账藏在埋葬名册里，失踪者家属与堡方都有取回它的理由。','Supply records lie among burial rolls; missing soldiers’ relatives and the keep each want them.','进入需处理守墓人的许可与塌方风险；带走骨殖不等同普通拾荒。','Entry involves the keeper’s consent and collapse risks. Human remains are not ordinary salvage.'),
('沉钟林口','Sunkenbell Verge','灰白树干间悬着一口没有钟舌的铜钟，林外摊贩卖蘑菇和干袜。','A clapperless bronze bell hangs among pale trunks; stalls outside sell mushrooms and dry socks.','采药人说听见钟声，樵夫说只是地底水；两人的路线并不相同。','Herbalists report bells; woodcutters blame underground water. They took different paths.','问清来源再入林，买补给也可闲逛；森林没有为玩家专设的必经考验。','Check accounts before entering or simply buy supplies; the forest has no compulsory hero trial.'),
('根桥聚落','Rootbridge Enclave','活树根跨过溪谷，树屋下也有石匠搭的普通仓房，精灵小孩用炭画风筝。','Living roots bridge a ravine above ordinary stone storehouses; elven children draw kites in charcoal.','老树根病变，议者争论是保旧桥还是给外来石匠一次机会。','An old bridge root is diseased; residents debate tradition against an outsider mason’s proposal.','可学药草与自然法术，但居民的家与圣地不是访客免费取材区。','Herbal and nature training is possible; homes and sacred groves are not free supply caches.'),
('鹿角泉','Antler Spring','泉眼四周堆着鹿蜕角与小石，水面倒影比林间日光明亮一些。','Shed antlers and pebbles ring water whose reflection seems brighter than the forest light.','上游洗矿的泥水威胁泉质，德鲁伊需要可追溯的样本而不是罪名。','Upstream mine washing threatens the water; druids need traceable samples rather than accusations.','取水、疗养、比对样本都有条件；泉水并非无限免费回满生命的机关。','Water collection, rest and sampling have limits; this is no infinite full-heal device.'),
('空心榆集','Hollow Elm Fair','空心榆的洞里传出笛声，地精铺开的布上既有铜钮，也有认真写价的工具。','Flutes sound within the hollow elm; goblin stalls display buttons and carefully priced tools.','邻村失物混在二手货里，卖主也可能是善意购得。','A village keepsake appears among secondhand goods; its seller may have bought it honestly.','可买卖、查来源或听歌；盗贼技巧不授予公开偷窃后毫无后果的特权。','Trade, trace provenance or enjoy music. Thieving skills do not erase consequences.'),
('沉钟沼','Sunkenbell Marsh','浅水下的钟沿覆着苔藓，木桩只露出半尺，蛙鸣一阵阵停下。','Moss covers a submerged bell rim; short posts rise through water as frogs fall suddenly quiet.','有人拆钟卖铜，有人认为这样会引灾；真正的风险先是淤泥与腐木。','Some strip the bell for copper, others predict disaster. Mud and rotten timber are immediate dangers.','调查可选择保全、留标或取样，危险不会按玩家等级自动变软。','Preserve, mark or sample the site; danger does not scale down for an inexperienced visitor.'),
('长眠树庭','Longsleep Grove','老树枝条挂着逝者木牌，风吹过时不是哭声，而是许多人家的门牌相碰。','Wooden memorial tags hang from old branches, sounding like household signs in the wind.','失土者要取回祖辈的牌，守林者担心取走会抹掉混居旧史。','Displaced families seek ancestral tags; guardians fear losing the record of a once-mixed community.','可查口述、复制铭文、协商迁葬；任何一方都不掌握所有祖先的答案。','Gather accounts, copy inscriptions and negotiate. Neither party knows every ancestor’s story.'),
('铜脊矿城','Copperback','高架矿车越过街面，炉火把雪照成橙色，地面店铺也卖鲜花和儿童木偶。','Ore carts cross above streets, furnace light colors snow orange, and shops sell flowers and puppets.','矿城富裕却缺干净水，深炉诸家争通风费用，工人家属要求先修病房。','Prosperity coexists with dirty water; houses debate ventilation bills while families demand a clinic.','可接修理活、学锻造、购装备；进入深井需实际许可与准备。','Repair work, smithing and equipment trade are available; deep shafts require permission and preparation.'),
('深炉议厅','Deephearth Hall','五张不同高度的椅子围着同一块旧砧，记录员用粉笔擦掉刚被否决的数额。','Five unequal chairs surround an old anvil while a clerk erases a rejected figure.','诸家并非铁板一块，继承人与工匠代表对欠薪和扩井意见相左。','Heirs and craft delegates disagree over arrears and expansion; the houses are not unanimous.','旁听资格与投票资格不同；帮一家做事不会自动成为另一家的死敌。','Listening is not voting; working for one house need not make another an enemy.'),
('七号通风井','Vent Shaft Seven','井口的布条向内飘，铁梯上结着水珠，底下有人敲三短一长。','Ribbons pull inward at the mouth; water beads on ladders above three short knocks and one long.','通风轮损坏，值班工头不愿停产，井下工人已开始头痛。','A fan is damaged. A foreman resists closure while workers develop headaches.','修复要工具与金属，封井保护生命但影响工资；空口施法不替代材料结算。','Repairs need tools and metal; closure saves lives but costs wages. Spells do not bypass material costs.'),
('盐晶洞','Saltglass Cavern','盐晶如结霜的玻璃，矿灯影子在壁上分成三层，滴水声听起来近在耳边。','Salt crystals resemble frosted glass, lamps cast triple shadows, and distant drops sound close.','稀有盐可制药，也可能破坏地下河；不同采法留下不同损害。','Rare salts aid medicines but mining may damage an underground river; methods have different costs.','可测绘、少量取样或接护送；不用假设所有矿物都能卖同一高价。','Survey, sample sparingly or escort crews; not every stone has the same valuable market.'),
('冷锤工坊','Coldhammer Workshop','年轻铁匠用脚踩风箱，旁边老师傅将一把漂亮却歪的刀重新放回火里。','An apprentice works the bellows as a master returns a beautiful but crooked blade to the fire.','炉炭涨价，店里在军单与农具之间排工期。','Charcoal costs rise; military orders compete with farming tools for forge time.','学习与制作各需真实时长，维修、改制可以按已知方法继续发展。','Training and crafting each take real time; repairs and adaptations follow known methods.'),
('矿灯旧轨','Lantern Rail','废轨穿过山腹，木车上还留着上一班矿工带来的酸面包。','Abandoned rails cross the mountain; a cart still holds a miner’s sour bread.','旧轨可通另一河谷，但地籍权属与坍塌段让捷径不是天然公共路。','The rail reaches another valley, but disputed ownership and collapse make it no automatic public shortcut.','查清支架后可提出复通方案，也可只救人离开，不强制接管矿业。','Inspect supports and propose reopening, or rescue someone and leave; no one must run a mine.'),
('镜湖镇','Mirrorlake','湖面映着三座能看见的塔，其余六塔在不同岸边，鱼市比学宫更早开门。','Three visible towers reflect in the lake; six stand elsewhere, and the fish market opens before the academy.','议会要求测水，渔户要求解释封湖范围，双方疲于被谣言代言。','The council needs water readings; fishers need clear closure boundaries, not rumors.','可学基础符文、做抄写或随船测量；普通求学不要求终身效忠。','Study runes, copy texts or join a survey boat; ordinary study requires no lifelong allegiance.'),
('第六观星塔','Sixth Observatory','屋顶铜环慢慢转，楼梯间堆着水桶，学徒正在擦昨夜漏下的雨。','Copper rings turn on the roof while apprentices mop rainwater from the stair.','星图有一块被旧抄本误记，学者的声誉与航船安全同时受影响。','A copied star chart contains an error affecting a scholar’s reputation and ships at sea.','观察、核对和讨论会改变认知，不会自动赋予预知未来的神力。','Observation and comparison change understanding, not grant prophecy.'),
('渡烛书院','Candleford School','长桌上蜡痕层层叠叠，有成年人跟孩子一起临摹同一排字。','Layers of wax cover desks where adults and children practice the same letters.','书院缺纸，贵族捐款附带只教本族人的条件。','Paper is scarce; a noble donor wants lessons restricted to one people.','可筹材料、授课、拒绝附带条件；知识来源须实际获得，抄本不等于掌握。','Supply materials, teach or contest the terms. Owning a copy is not mastering its contents.'),
('裂纹温室','Cracked Glasshouse','玻璃拼补成彩色屋顶，枝条缠着暖管，蜂箱旁放着避火砂。','Patched colored glass roofs vines around warm pipes; sand stands ready beside the hives.','一株疗伤植物需要删枝，药剂师与保种者对取舍不同。','A medicinal plant needs pruning; medicine makers and seed keepers favor different cuts.','药剂与符材有真实产量和消耗，不能因植物神奇便无限取用。','Reagents and medicines have yields and costs; magic plants are not unlimited stock.'),
('无声渡台','Quiet Landing','石阶直入湖水，水鸟从不用这块台面，船家说是风向而不是咒语。','Steps vanish into the lake; birds avoid the landing, which boatmen blame on wind rather than curses.','送往塔中的封箱没有按时签收，是否开启牵涉隐私与危险。','A sealed shipment lacks its receipt; opening it raises questions of privacy and risk.','运送、查交接人或求助专家都可行；封印知识要与真正见过的内容区分。','Deliver, trace handlers or ask a specialist; distinguish seal lore from contents actually seen.'),
('倒影试场','Reflections Yard','石池把人影照成扭曲长线，空靶边有一块写着停手信号的木牌。','Pools stretch reflections into lines; a sign beside empty targets explains the stop signal.','学徒想证明新法，监督者担心旁观者站得太近。','An apprentice wants to prove a new spell; a supervisor worries about nearby spectators.','法术试验先谈风险、目标与耗材；控制、护持和远距技巧不等于全能改写现实。','Agree risks, targets and reagents before testing. Control, protection and range are bounded abilities.'),
('无名王庭外城','Outer Nameless Court','城门王号被凿去，卖热饼的摊位靠着断裂登基碑，婚礼队伍照常经过。','Royal names are chiseled from the gate; hotbread stalls lean against a broken coronation stone as weddings pass.','三位自称继承人的使者争修城门的署名，居民只想别再漏风。','Three claimants dispute credit for gate repairs; residents mainly want the drafts stopped.','可谋生、查家史或介入政治，不必恢复帝国也能有完整人生。','Earn a living, trace family history or enter politics; restoring the empire is optional.'),
('失名档案院','House of Lost Names','档案柜以气味分区，湿纸、羊皮和防虫草混在一起，空抽屉比满柜更醒目。','Damp paper, vellum and herbs scent the cabinets; empty drawers stand out more than full shelves.','书记发现两份继承文书互相矛盾，却不知道哪份在流亡途中被补写。','Two inheritance documents conflict; a clerk cannot tell which was amended in exile.','比对墨、证人和保存过程，不把读者的推断写成既定真相。','Compare ink, witnesses and custody; a reader’s theory is not established truth.'),
('裂冠广场','Splitcrown Square','喷泉中央的王冠分成五块，卖花人用其中一块压住收摊的布。','The fountain crown lies in five pieces; a flower seller uses one to weigh down a cloth.','各家纪念仪式撞了日子，街坊反对被迫选边才准摆摊。','Commemorations overlap; shopkeepers object to choosing sides just to trade.','可以组织共用场地、摆摊或围观；仪式与承诺须区分。','Arrange shared space, trade or watch; attending a ceremony is not automatically swearing allegiance.'),
('黑蜡下街','Blackwax Understreet','灯铺收旧蜡再熬，低门后的乐声与争吵相隔不过一道薄墙。','Candle shops remelt old wax; music and arguments live one thin wall apart.','消息贩卖者知道一条入口，却也有必须隐瞒的债主。','An information broker knows an entrance and has a creditor to avoid.','可谈价、互助、调查或拒绝；偷听得到的是某人的说法而非全知旁白。','Bargain, help, investigate or refuse; overheard words are claims, not omniscient narration.'),
('沉王水宫','Drowned King’s Hall','水淹到石狮膝盖，旧席位高低不齐，铜门背后有规律的敲击。','Water reaches stone lions’ knees; uneven seats face a bronze door and measured knocking.','宫中水位受城市排水影响，抢取遗物可能让外城低洼区遭殃。','Water levels depend on city drainage; removing relics may flood low outer streets.','测水、排险、保全与离开都有意义，发现王冠不强迫进入结局。','Survey, make safe, preserve or leave. Finding a crown never forces an ending.'),
('无火旧宫灶','Cold Palace Kitchens','十二口巨锅空着，侍从后人的小灶却在角落熬豆，烟从破天窗钻出去。','Twelve great kettles stand empty while descendants of servants cook beans beneath a broken skylight.','旧宫粮库的最后钥匙属于一位不愿卖掉记忆的老人。','The last granary key belongs to an elder unwilling to sell her memories.','可以帮修屋顶、听旧事、商量借钥匙；王庭遗产不只属于显赫姓氏。','Repair the roof, hear stories or negotiate a loan; imperial heritage belongs to more than famous names.'),
('雾湾港','Mistbay Harbor','船壳像山丘靠在雾里，海鸥落在新旧两种海关旗之间。','Hulls loom like hills in mist; gulls perch between old and new customs flags.','海路偏航让货物到得迟，港务官与灯塔守望者互相追问。','Navigational errors delay cargo; harbor officers and beacon keepers seek answers from each other.','可谋水手生计、修索具、护送和换取消息，船期不会为主角暂停。','Work aboard ship, repair rigging, escort or seek news; sailing schedules do not pause for the hero.'),
('最后古灯塔','Last Ancient Beacon','塔壁没有砖缝，海盐积在凹槽里，灯室只亮着一束缓慢转动的细光。','The seamless tower is salted along its grooves; one thin beam turns slowly in the lantern room.','旧灯心衰弱，拆换可恢复航标，却可能丢掉它保存的古代回声。','The core is fading. Replacement may restore navigation while destroying ancient recorded echoes.','学者、海员与守望者各有所求；修复要有真实材料，点灯不是预定终局。','Scholars, sailors and keepers want different things. Repairs consume materials; relighting is no final victory.'),
('风骨盐场','Windbone Saltpans','木风车嘎吱响，盐工把盐铲成鱼骨形，落日映得眼睛发痛。','Wooden windmills creak as workers rake salt into fishbone patterns that glare at sunset.','盐商压价，工人怕停工便付不起渔船债。','Buyers cut prices; workers fear a stoppage would leave fishing debts unpaid.','贸易、运货、工具改进可交织，利害并非简单善恶二选一。','Trade, hauling and better tools intersect; interests do not divide neatly into good and evil.'),
('破帆泊地','Torn Sail Anchorage','难民把旧帆缝成棚，夜里有人照旧教孩子跳远方家乡的舞。','Refugees stitch old sails into shelters and teach children dances from distant homes.','失土盟约想登记失散者，有人担心名单落到旧仇手里。','The Lostlands Covenant records missing families; some fear the list reaching old enemies.','可送物资、找人或帮助保密，不把受助者写成只会感谢的布景。','Bring supplies, search or protect privacy; aid recipients have lives beyond gratitude.'),
('潮鸣洞','Tidesong Cave','潮声沿石孔发出低音，晒干的海草系在安全线两端。','Tides hum through stone holes; dried kelp marks both ends of a safety rope.','走私船曾藏过货，退潮时只剩几枚刻号铜扣，不能据此指控所有港工。','Smugglers once stored cargo here; numbered buckles are clues, not evidence against all dockworkers.','等待合适潮位或带齐绳灯再查，时间与补给来自同一正式旅程。','Wait for the tide or bring rope and light; time and supplies belong to the same real journey.'),
('远礁祈潮所','Farreef Shrine','木台挂着海员留下的结绳，祭司把每根绳的主人名字记在小册里。','Sailors leave knotted cords on a platform; a priest records each owner’s name.','一根新绳冒用了死者名字，可能是求庇护，也可能是诈骗。','A fresh cord bears a dead sailor’s name, perhaps seeking sanctuary, perhaps fraud.','查名、护送和谈判皆可，祝祷不承诺天气或命运为玩家让路。','Trace the name, escort or negotiate; blessings promise no control over weather or fate.'),
('灰穗集','Greygrain Market','麦袋之间穿过修锅匠、赶羊人和唱旧歌的旅人，粮秤由两个人一起抬。','Tinkers, herders and old-song singers pass among grain sacks; two people carry the great scale.','旱地歉收、河地丰收，统一粮价掩盖不同村庄的损失。','Dry fields failed while riverside crops prospered; a single grain price hides unequal losses.','可买卖、做农活、查量器或住下，不必每次进镇便卷入政变。','Trade, farm, inspect measures or settle in; a town visit need not trigger a coup.'),
('缝旗营','Patchbanner Camp','不同旗色缝成一面遮阳篷，流亡者用失去的村名给新街道命名。','Many banner colors form one awning; exiles name new lanes after lost villages.','失土盟约内部争论重返故地还是扎根这里，年轻人与长者都不一致。','The Covenant debates return against settlement; neither the young nor the old agree among themselves.','参与救济、学手艺、记录地契与选择离开都合理，效忠不是领取帮助的唯一条件。','Aid, crafts, deeds and departure are all possible; allegiance is not the only price of help.'),
('晴风果园','Fairwind Orchard','果树绑着旧铃铛，午后有人把伤枝削成孩子的玩具。','Old bells hang from fruit trees; damaged branches become children’s toys in the afternoon.','半身人果农遭霉病，巫师的试验药可能有效却需要先小块试用。','Halfling growers face blight; an experimental treatment needs a small trial before wider use.','采果、试验、售卖与闲谈可连成日常，成功也不是永不再有坏收成。','Picking, trials, sales and conversation make a life; success guarantees no perfect future harvest.'),
('旧龙骨渠','Old Dragonbone Channel','石渠沿巨大白骨弯曲，村人用它当桥，也争论那是否真是龙骨。','A stone channel follows huge pale bones used as a bridge; villagers disagree whether they are truly draconic.','渠首漏水，挖骨卖钱可能救眼前急，却会破坏水路支撑。','The headgate leaks. Selling the bones could raise money while weakening the waterway.','可修闸、求援、研究或改线；传说先当传说，确认后才成为新事实。','Repair, seek aid, study or reroute. Legend remains legend until evidence establishes more.'),
('风铃丘','Windchime Hill','丘上每户都挂不同音的风铃，夜行者凭声音认路而不是看旗。','Every house hangs a different chime; night travelers navigate by sound rather than flags.','兽裔与人类共同守路，一封恐吓信试图让他们互疑。','Beastkin and humans guard the road together; a threatening letter seeks to divide them.','可查笔迹、陪巡或照常做生意，不预设某种族天生忠诚或邪恶。','Examine the hand, patrol or keep trading; no people are born loyal or wicked.'),
('春雪修院','Springsnow Hospice','院子晾满染过药汁的布，灶房给病人、护工和过客煮同一锅浓粥。','Medicinal cloths dry in the yard; one thick porridge feeds patients, carers and travelers.','修院药房缺盐与酒精，捐助者想优先治疗自己的部下。','The dispensary lacks salts and spirits; a patron wants his own followers treated first.','可学急救、采药、运物或守夜；治病不凭善意保证成功，伤势按正式记录延续。','Learn first aid, gather herbs, deliver or keep watch; good intentions guarantee no cure, and injuries persist.')]
FACTIONS = [
('white-thorn','白棘骑士团','White Thorn Order','守住道路和停战誓言的跨族骑士团，靠农庄、护送与捐助维持，不代表一切善。','A cross-people order defending roads and truces, sustained by farms, escorts and donations, not the embodiment of all good.','团长想保住补给，教头想保住新兵，礼拜堂想先辨认死者；内部可以公开争论。','Its commander needs supplies, instructors need recruits alive, and the chapel wants the dead identified. Internal disagreement is real.'),
('nine-towers','九塔议会','Nine Towers Council','学社、工坊与观测站组成的议会，拥有知识也受制于资金、失误与地方同意。','A council of schools, workshops and observatories, rich in knowledge but constrained by money, mistakes and local consent.','开放抄本者与主张封存危险技术者常争执；没有一个全知总法师替全体说话。','Open-copy advocates dispute custodians of dangerous knowledge; no omniscient archmage speaks for all.'),
('ashriver-league','烬河自由盟','Ashriver Free League','渡口、集镇与独立农户结成的松散联盟，重交易与地方自治，也会偏袒熟人。','A loose league of ferries, towns and free farms, valuing trade and local rule while remaining vulnerable to favoritism.','大商队要稳定关税，小船户要减免，镇民怕账目公开后有人报复。','Large caravans want stable tolls, small boatmen want exemptions, and residents fear reprisals over public accounts.'),
('deephearth','深炉诸家','Deephearth Houses','守有矿井、炉坊和旧契约的矮人家族联盟，成员与雇工不限族属。','Dwarven houses holding mines, forges and old contracts; neither membership nor employment is restricted to ancestry.','继承权、工匠资格和工伤抚养常冲突，矿主与矿工不会被一句祖训统一。','Inheritance, craft standing and injury support collide; an ancestral saying cannot unite owners and workers.'),
('lostlands','失土盟约','Lostlands Covenant','由流亡者、失地军户与迁徙聚落维系的互助盟约，既有人要归乡，也有人只求安居。','An aid covenant of exiles, displaced military households and migrants, divided between return and a new home.','名单能找亲人也能追人，地契能保记忆也会排斥如今住在地上的家庭。','Lists can reunite or endanger families; deeds preserve memory while threatening those now living on the land.'),
('rootkeepers','根桥守林会','Rootbridge Keepers','精灵、兽裔与人类共同维护的林地习惯法社群，重水源与互惠。','Elves, beastkin and humans share woodland customs centered on water and reciprocity.','守旧仪式与救急工程之间没有一条永远正确的线。','No permanent rule settles every tension between old rites and urgent engineering.'),
('beaconwatch','古灯守望社','Old Beacon Watch','灯塔守望者与沿海船户的自愿互助社，不拥有所有灯塔，也不知全部秘密。','A voluntary fellowship of beacon keepers and coastal crews, owning neither every beacon nor every secret.','航标安全与古代记忆保存有时需要取舍。','Navigation and preservation of ancient memories can demand different repairs.'),
('blackwax','黑蜡同行','Blackwax Fellowship','锁匠、跑腿人、地下向导和窃贼混杂的互保圈子，靠名声而非统一王法。','A mutual-protection circle of locksmiths, runners, guides and thieves, governed by reputation rather than one criminal king.','守口如瓶不能变成包庇一切，成员会拒绝让家人受害的委托。','Discretion is not unconditional complicity; members may refuse work that endangers their families.'),
('springhospice','春雪修院同工','Springsnow Carers','治病、安葬、抄书与收留旅人的松散宗教共同体，各人信仰并不完全相同。','A loose religious community of healers, burial keepers, copyists and hosts, not uniform in belief.','匮乏时谁先用药必须面对具体病情，不能按捐钱多少假装没有争议。','Scarcity forces difficult triage; donations do not erase the ethical dispute.'),
('greygrain','灰穗合仓','Greygrain Granary Union','自由农与佃农共建的储粮合作，仓钥由不同行当轮流保管。','Free farmers and tenants pool grain under keys held by different trades.','诚实的歉收报告可能使村庄借不到钱，隐瞒又会伤害邻村。','An honest crop report may block credit, while concealment harms neighbors.'),
('courtwards','外城街坊会','Outer Ward Assembly','住在帝国遗址上的普通家庭共同修路、守夜、办婚丧，不以复辟为唯一愿望。','Families living amid imperial ruins repair lanes, keep watch and hold weddings without necessarily wanting restoration.','继承人的宣言只有落到漏水的屋顶和粮价上，才会有人认真听。','Claimants earn attention only when speeches reach leaking roofs and food prices.'),
('saltroad','盐路车队','Saltroad Caravans','由独立车主结伴的商旅联盟，运盐、纸、药和人员，利润并不均分。','Independent wagon owners travel together carrying salt, paper, medicine and passengers, with unequal profits.','守约、改道与亏本之间时有冲突，车队不是无条件听命的玩家仓库。','Promises, detours and losses collide; a caravan is not the player’s obedient storage chest.')]
